  {
    "episode_id": 65911,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/5/65911.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 47,
    "turn_text": "Well, a couple things. First of all, I'm glad he never mentioned impeachment. I think the Democrats thought he was going to talk about that. He never talked about that, which I think says a lot about him. But he focused on three areas that I think we have been successful in in this country. The economy and where we're at with a record level of prosperity, more people working in this country than ever before. We've moved 7 million people off food stamps, and there is a recognition with low unemployment that this country is back economically. And that's a positive thing. Secondarily on trade. Our farmers, our manufacturers rely on international trade and today we have four trade agreements with our four largest trading partners, Mexico, Canada, China, Japan. And how important that is in a country where we're only four and a half percent percent of the world's population. And so trade equals jobs and economic opportunities in central, west central, Illinois, but also across the country. And then I thought on national security, the president did an excellent job talking about taking out albagati and taking out sumamani to terrorists that have hurt Americans. And I thought he we've been uh... you know that uh... the the family uh... up in the balcony particularly the young woman who was killed by albaghdadi murdered by this terrace and the fact that america safer because our military took out these two terrorists and i think that was inspiring uh... and i think it said uh... a lot the president delivered the speech while he stepped to the teleprompter and then lastly particularly at the end that played he talked about the fabric of America and our best days are ahead of us. And that was really inspirational in talking about the greatness of America in a really bipartisan way. And then lastly, he talked about our challenges to the future, which clearly we have some deficiencies and things we have to work on in a bipartisan way.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The president did not mention impeachment during his speech.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The U.S. has four active trade agreements with its four largest trading partners: Mexico, Canada, China, and Japan.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The president successfully targeted and eliminated al-Baghdadi and Sumari, key terrorist figures.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The U.S. economy has reached a record level of prosperity.",
