    "conversation_move_label": "Topic Shift"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 65911,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/5/65911.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 51,
    "turn_text": "Well, listen, raising that last night using her and her mother, who has sacrificed so much as an example, I think highlights the need for giving students a choice, particularly in our urban areas. Through no fault of their own, sometimes they're born into poverty and the circumstances that don't allow them to go to the best schools. But talking about school choice, talking about these opportunity scholarships, has to continue to be part of the dialogue. It was ironic that even Nancy Pelosi did not stand up, did not clap for that young girl. And the opportunity she's going to have with school choice. And this should not be a partisan issue. It really shouldn't. This should be an American issue. But I think you're going to find Republicans continue to be supportive of that. Hopefully we can find some like-minded Democrats. They want to come on to help young women, young girls like her that we saw last night and thought the president did a good job in highlighting that.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
